+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,4 +15,17 @@ It throws a `SyntaxError` (a `TypeError` for a non-string) when the pointer is n
 `-` token (which names no existing element), or a step into a primitive. Only own members of objects
 are considered, so `/constructor` or `/length` never reach inherited properties.
 
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Patch (an array of `add`,
+`remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations) to a parsed JSON document and returns the
+result as a new value. Neither argument is mutated, and values taken from the patch are copied.
+
+It throws a `TypeError` when the patch is malformed (not an array, unknown `op`, missing `path`,
+`from` or `value`), a `SyntaxError` when a pointer is invalid, and a `RangeError` when an operation
+fails: unresolved target, out-of-range or non-canonical array index, removing the whole document,
+moving a value into its own child, or a `test` that does not match. The patch is atomic: on any
+error nothing is returned. Pointers follow the rules above, so only own members are ever touched and
+`__proto__` is an ordinary member name.
+
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
